# NIZAM - environment template for the `signalbus` service. TEMPLATE ONLY. NOTHING HERE IS EXECUTED.
#
# Owning contract: PFOS 12 - Two-Agent VPS Deployment & Operations, §4.1 (the append-only store and
#   its internal-only binding), §4.5.3 (the default consent scope), §2.2.5/§2.2.6 (never published,
#   and refused at the network layer rather than authenticated on a reachable port), §3.2.7 (one
#   environment file per service), §7.6 (this path).
# Spec: .kiro/specs/06-two-agent-vps/ - task 7.3. Contract 12, phase 7. Requirements R7, R8, R9, R23,
#   R24.
# Steering: .kiro/steering/two-agent-vps.md §0b, §2 (writing this file is permitted, running it is
#   not), §4.2 (the bus is the only channel between the agents), §7 (placeholders only, AC09).
# Binding requirement: ops/BUS_NETWORK_BINDING.md - items 1-5 are structural in
#   ops/docker-compose.yml; this file adds no entry that could soften any of them.
#
# Companion: ops/docker-compose.yml declares this file as this service's single env_file, under the
#   placeholder <BUS_ENV_PATH>. Audited by src/server/ops/envTemplates.ts.
#
# HOW TO READ AN ENTRY. Each assignment is preceded by exactly three annotation lines:
#   what:    one line saying what the value is
#   gate:    which human gate in ops/GATE_REGISTER.md supplies it - G1..G8, or `operator` for a
#            value the operator simply chooses, or `build` for a path to an artefact the build emits
#   secret:  yes if disclosing the value would let someone reach or impersonate this deployment
#
# EVERY VALUE IS AN <ANGLE_BRACKET> PLACEHOLDER WHOSE NAME IS ITS OWN ENTRY NAME.
#
# THIS FILE IS SHORT ON PURPOSE. The bus is the narrowest service in the deployment: it accepts an
# envelope that has no field capable of carrying a figure, a date, an identifier, or a narrative
# (§4.3), and it serves that envelope back subject to two independent gates. Nothing about that is
# configurable, so there is nothing here to configure it with.

# what: the absolute directory the append-only signal store and its audit mirror live in
# gate: G1
# secret: no
SIGNALS_DATA_DIR=<SIGNALS_DATA_DIR>

# what: the store file name within that directory
# gate: operator
# secret: no
SIGNALS_STORE_FILE=<SIGNALS_STORE_FILE>

# what: where this service listens on the internal network; the two agents are its only clients
# gate: operator
# secret: no
BUS_INTERNAL_ENDPOINT=<BUS_INTERNAL_ENDPOINT>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What is deliberately absent, and why absence is the mechanism rather than a gap
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. NO PUBLIC ADDRESS, PORT, OR HOSTNAME. Contract 12 §2.2.5 puts this service on an internal
#    network with no gateway, so there is nothing off-host to be reachable from and nothing to bind
#    publicly. An entry here that named a public interface would be the first half of the exposure
#    R9 forbids, and the correct failure is refusal at the network layer, not an authentication
#    check on a reachable port (§2.2.6).
#
# 2. NO DEFAULT CONSENT SCOPE ENTRY. §4.5.3 makes the default `producer_only` for any new signal
#    kind until the owner explicitly widens it, and the port configuration encodes that as a
#    single-member literal type rather than as a setting (src/server/ports/signalBus.ts). A
#    configurable default would let a deployment widen consent without a code review, which is
#    exactly the drift the single-member literal exists to prevent.
#
# 3. NO RETENTION ENTRY. Retention windows and pruning mechanics for every table belong to contract
#    06 §8, which also fixes the one rule a deployment could get wrong - the de-duplication window
#    is never pruned shorter than the provider's redelivery window. This template does not restate
#    it, because a value in two places is a value that can disagree with itself.
#
# 4. NO KILL SWITCH ENTRY. §8.2 names the two agents, the scheduler, and the backup service, and
#    ops/docker-compose.yml mounts the sentinel volume into exactly those four. A publish is halted
#    at the publisher, before the envelope is built, so halting the store as well would add a second
#    place for the halt to be wrong without closing anything the first place leaves open.
#
# 5. NO CREDENTIAL OF ANY KIND. This service holds no bot token, no model key, and no storage
#    credential. It is the one place in the deployment where both agents' state meets, so it is also
#    the one place where holding either agent's secret would be worst.
